**1 [[Cadaver Bear]] spawns.

==Strategy==
When you hit the base, make sure you do so with [[Talents|Talented]] [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]]. At the same time, prefire the Iron Wall Cannon. If you do everything correctly, everything annoying burrows, everything weak dies to Bahamut's Explosion, and Puffington gets hit twice and then hits the Iron Wall and nothing else. Bahamut will hit Puffington again, before getting knocked back by Puffington and landing the killing blow on him on the following rebound. Note that at Lv.40, Awakened Bahamut Cat needs an (Sm) Defense [[Cat Combo]] to survive a hit.

If you don't have Bahamut's Talents nor any unit that can deal with Cadaver Bear, you can use the Li'l Cyclone to stack up a bunch of attackers. After hitting the base, wait for Li'l Zyclone to burrow and then fire the Holy Blast cannon. Then, use units like [[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Mystic Uril]] or [[Hermit Cat (Special Cat)|Masked Grandmaster Cat]] to juggle Puffington while you use cat such as [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]] and [[Red Riding Mina (Special Cat)|Awakened Mina]] to deal damage to Cadaver Bear. Eventually, the Li'l Zyclone will die and everything will get killed by Puffington. At this point, try your best to stall and chip down both threats. Once either of the threats are down, it is almost a guaranteed win.

On higher crowned difficulties, the Awakened Bahamut strategy still works as long as you include [[Idi:N (Special Cat)|Idi:N2/NX]] to kill the Mr. Puffington.

